<DATA=Code>
  2009-01-01 12:00  => IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* SSG-4 (MT-056): one LECTIS for every call. Record length, key
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* position, mode (sequential list or key lookup), the COND test
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* and the Y2K key positions come from the SGSPARM file written
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* by the skeleton hand-off (LectisParm.ps1); see spec.md. The
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* data file is read sequentially in both modes (claim C3).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>* Print lines and DISPLAY texts as the skeleton.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => PROGRAM-ID. 'ASSURFED-UTILIT-LECTIS-GN'.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => CONFIGURATION SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SOURCE-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => OBJECT-COMPUTER. UNIVAC-1100-60EIS.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => SPECIAL-NAMES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     DECIMAL-POINT IS COMMA
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>         PAGE IS SAUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FILE-CONTROL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT PARMF ASSIGN TO DISC SGSPARM.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT LECIN ASSIGN TO DISC LECIN.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT LECCRD ASSIGN TO DISC LECCRD.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     SELECT IMP ASSIGN TO PRINTER.
