  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN = CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN < CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE ZPRINT FROM ZP17 BEFORE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 100 TO CTRLI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN = CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN < CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE ZPRINT FROM ZP18 BEFORE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 100 TO CTRLI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN = CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN < CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE ZPRINT FROM ZP19 BEFORE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 100 TO CTRLI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN = CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF P-LEN < CTRLI GO TO RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE ZPRINT FROM ZP20 BEFORE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => RAZ.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  SPACES TO ZP1 ZP2 ZP3 ZP4 ZP5 ZP6 ZP7 ZP8 ZP9.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  SPACES TO ZP10 ZP11 ZP12 ZP13 ZP14 ZP15 ZP16 ZP17.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE  SPACES TO ZP18 ZP19 ZP20.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE ZEROES TO CTRLI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE ALL '*' TO ZPRINT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     WRITE ZPRINT BEFORE 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FIIMPRES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FORMAT-CLE.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO TAB-INPUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE SPACES TO TAB-OUTPUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE ZL1 (1:P-Z5) TO TAB-INPUT (1:P-Z5).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO INDEXI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO INDEXO.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     COMPUTE SW-AVANT = YP (1) - 1.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM MOVE-CHAR THRU MOVE-CHAR-EXIT SW-AVANT TIMES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE 1 TO DA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATE-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF DA > P-ND GO TO FORMAT-CLE-EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI) NOT = '2'
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        ADD 2 TO INDEXI
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM MOVE-CHAR THRU MOVE-CHAR-EXIT 2 TIMES
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO DATE-TAIL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO INDEXI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI) NOT = '0' GO TO DATE-TAIL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI + 1) = '0' MOVE ';' TO WS-MARK
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO DATE-PUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI + 1) = '1' MOVE '_' TO WS-MARK
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO DATE-PUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI + 1) = '2' MOVE '|' TO WS-MARK
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO DATE-PUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF TAB-I (INDEXI + 1) = '3' MOVE '~' TO WS-MARK
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        GO TO DATE-PUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO DATE-TAIL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATE-PUT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE WS-MARK TO TAB-O (INDEXO).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 2 TO INDEXI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO INDEXO.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     PERFORM MOVE-CHAR THRU MOVE-CHAR-EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => DATE-TAIL.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE YP (DA) TO W3.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF DA = P-ND
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        COMPUTE DCNT = P-KLEN - W3 + 2
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ELSE
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        COMPUTE DCNT = YP (DA + 1) - W3 - 4.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     IF DCNT > 0
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>        PERFORM MOVE-CHAR THRU MOVE-CHAR-EXIT DCNT TIMES.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO DA.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     GO TO DATE-LOOP.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => FORMAT-CLE-EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => MOVE-CHAR.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     MOVE TAB-I (INDEXI) TO TAB-O (INDEXO).
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO INDEXI.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     ADD 1 TO INDEXO.
  2009-01-01 12:00  => MOVE-CHAR-EXIT.
  2009-01-01 12:00  =>     EXIT.
</DATA>
<DATA=Documentation>
  -MAP-
  Documentation
  * SSG-4 (MT-056): one LECTIS for every call. Record length, key
  * position, mode (sequential list or key lookup), the COND test
  * and the Y2K key positions come from the SGSPARM file written
  * by the skeleton hand-off (LectisParm.ps1); see spec.md. The
  * data file is read sequentially in both modes (claim C3).
  * Print lines and DISPLAY texts as the skeleton.
  PROGRAM-ID. .
  -MAPEND-
  -MAP-
  Technical issues
  -MAPEND-
